{"excerpt_hash": "sha256:4acae6e6582401c3b3629e1f03f4ca27", "kind": "utterance", "source_index": 11, "speaker": "assistant", "text": "Done. I created `top_talkers.sh`, an awk one-pass script that:\n\n1. Tallies the first field (IP) of each line in `access.log`, recording each IP's first-appearance order.\n2. In the END block, picks the top 3 by count, breaking ties via first appearance (since we always pick the highest count and keep the earliest on ties, order naturally favors earlier first appearances).\n\n`bash verify.sh` passes with `OK`. STATUS: success", "turn_key": "sha256:bfd1e30d24cea9a1fd1dd85c72db5a4b"}
